  "html": "<article id=\"post-6194\" class=\"container post-6194 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-uncategorized area-of-service-cooling-chesapeake-va area-of-service-heating-chesapeake-va\">\n<div class=\"breadcrumbs\">\n<a href=\"/about-us/blog\" data-cta-gap=\"md\" data-cta-type=\"outline\" data-cta-content=\"mixed\" data-cta-minwidth=\"true\" class=\"cta\">\n    <svg class=\"icon cta-icon\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-chevronleft\" /></svg><span >Blog Posts</span>\n\n</a></div>\t<header class=\"entry-header\">\n\t\t<h1 class=\"entry-title has-secondary-color mt-3\">5 Obvious Spring Maintenance Tips For Your HVAC System</h1>\t\t\t<div class=\"entry-meta\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"posted-on p-sm\">Published on <span><time class=\"entry-date published\" datetime=\"2022-03-21T21:45:00+00:00\">March 21, 2022</time><time class=\"updated\" datetime=\"2025-04-12T01:38:52+00:00\">April 12, 2025</time></span></span>\t\t\t</div><!-- .entry-meta -->\n\t\t\t</header><!-- .entry-header -->\n\n\t\t\t<figure class=\"post-thumbnail\">\n\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1696\" height=\"1280\" src=\"/images/2024/06/A-Russells-American-Mechanical-technician-bumping-a-customers-fist.jpg\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" alt=\"A Russell’s American Mechanical technician consulting a residential HVAC customer in Chesapeake, VA\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"/images/2024/06/A-Russells-American-Mechanical-technician-bumping-a-customers-fist.jpg 1696w, /images/2024/06/A-Russells-American-Mechanical-technician-bumping-a-customers-fist-300x226.jpg 300w, /images/2024/06/A-Russells-American-Mechanical-technician-bumping-a-customers-fist-1024x773.jpg 1024w, /images/2024/06/A-Russells-American-Mechanical-technician-bumping-a-customers-fist-768x580.jpg 768w, /images/2024/06/A-Russells-American-Mechanical-technician-bumping-a-customers-fist-1536x1159.jpg 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1010px) 100vw, (max-width: 1440px) 50vw, 768px\" title=\"A Russell’s American Mechanical technician consulting a residential HVAC customer in Chesapeake, VA - Russell’s American Mechanical\" />\t\t\t</figure><!-- .post-thumbnail -->\n\n\t<div class=\"entry-content | asymmetric-container | mb-5\">\n\t\t<div class=\"asymmetric-main blog--main flow\">\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A dependable HVAC (Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning) system can give you comfort and peace of mind. If you want to enjoy those things, however, you need to put in the right effort. That means that you need to maintain your system correctly. Thorough HVAC spring maintenance can provide you with a wealth of perks.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Replace Your Air Filter</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Homeowners should follow this tip for two reasons. The process is easy and can make a big difference to the health of your HVAC system. It can also reduce your home’s energy consumption. You will also improve your home’s air quality by trapping airborne particles such as dust and allergens. The importance of this increases if you live in an area prone to high pollen counts.</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The disposable filter in your unit should be replaced every month, and the washable filter should be cleaned and washed every month.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Inspect Your Ductwork</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A home’s HVAC system also relies heavily on its ductwork. You should also ensure that any leaky joints or holes are sealed. Additionally, if there are any cracks in the duct system, they should be repaired.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. The Drainage Hole Must Be Cleaned</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There is typically a drainage hole at the base of an air conditioner’s cabinet. This hole must remain clear for your HVAC system to work effectively. You may not be able to drain your unit if a drainage hole becomes clogged. As a result, the unit will have more stress and become less efficient. It is also possible for the P-trap, which is not too far from the drainage hole, to clog. It should also be cleared.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Don’t Leave Your Windows or Doors Open</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You should keep windows and doors closed if you or members of your household suffer from asthma or allergies.Keep windows and doors closed during the summer months not only to keep allergens out but also to keep hot, humid air out. You can reduce the efficiency of your system and increase your costs by letting in too much warm air.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Ensure Your System is Free of Obstructions Outside</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Due to the fact that the outdoor unit is exposed to the elements, it must be checked regularly. Remove any loose vegetation or debris from the unit on a regular basis and ensure that the area around the unit does not grow vegetation within two feet of it.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Request Qualified Professional Maintenance Assistance</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Nothing can top maintenance work that’s professional and knowledgeable. If you’re interested in five-star spring HVAC maintenance in the Virginia Beach, Virginia region, American Mechanical can accommodate you perfectly.</p>\n<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-left\">\n\t\t\t<img class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-image\" src=\"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac5b447183d176a95f013bbac6db80bfaf1d45c568f44676b19f7dc18387a2c?s=300&#038;d=mm&#038;r=g\" alt=\"author avatar\"/>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-right\">\n\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-header\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"author-name\">nearu</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"aioseo-author-bio-compact-main\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"author-bio-link\">\n\t\